(Seen by thing_cycle_across_a_see.vox. Read on its own this file is legal:
 `hoop` is defined before the `ring` that holds one. Spliced into a file that
 already defines `ring`, the two halves close a cycle - which is why the
 rules have to be read against the whole program rather than one file.)

A thing called hoop has
  a number called thickness is 0.

A thing called ring has
  a hoop called rim.
